WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.378 --> 00:00:01.211
- Hello.

00:00:01.211 --> 00:00:02.501
- [Narrator] Normally
when you think of words,

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.120
they fit into a language.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.981
- Bonjour.

00:00:04.981 --> 00:00:06.661
- [Narrator] But there's
a relatively new class

00:00:06.661 --> 00:00:08.921
of words that don't quite follow the rules

00:00:08.921 --> 00:00:11.171
and it's called wasei-eigo.

00:00:14.372 --> 00:00:16.092
John Kelly is a language writer.

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:17.792
- [John] I spend a lot of my time

00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:19.384
writing about word origins.

00:00:19.384 --> 00:00:21.723
- [Narrator] He's a linguistics
expert and he knows just

00:00:21.723 --> 00:00:25.053
about everything about the
phenomenon called wasei-eigo.

00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:30.024
- [John] Wasei-eigo literally
means Japan-made English.

00:00:30.024 --> 00:00:34.944
It is a language process
that takes foreign words,

00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:38.613
usually English words
and transmogrifies them

00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:42.780
into something wholly new and
novel for Japanese purposes.

00:00:43.991 --> 00:00:46.972
We see this with a word like karaoke.

00:00:46.972 --> 00:00:49.123
Everybody knows and
everybody loves karaoke,

00:00:49.123 --> 00:00:52.483
but it joins the Japanese
kara, which means empty

00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:55.792
and oke, which is a Japanese
rendering of orchestra.

00:00:55.792 --> 00:00:58.293
So a karaoke is an empty orchestra.

00:00:58.293 --> 00:01:00.824
- [Narrator] The most popular
example is the word Pokémon.

00:01:00.824 --> 00:01:02.752
- [John] The creator of Pokémon took

00:01:02.752 --> 00:01:05.384
two English words, pocket and monster.

00:01:05.384 --> 00:01:08.563
He smashed them together and got Pokémon.

00:01:08.563 --> 00:01:10.881
- [Narrator] Or take cosplay,
a word that describes

00:01:10.881 --> 00:01:13.181
people dressing up as
fictional characters.

00:01:13.181 --> 00:01:15.771
- [John] Cosplay joins costume and play.

00:01:15.771 --> 00:01:16.933
- [Narrator] And there's anime.

00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:18.923
- [John] Anime is a
fairly straight forward

00:01:18.923 --> 00:01:21.683
rendering of the English animation.

00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:24.853
Wasei-eigo is important
because language is always

00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:27.069
changing and reinventing itself.

00:01:27.069 --> 00:01:29.333
- [Narrator] What new words
will pop up in the future?

00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:31.000
Only time will tell.

